00:00:55.687 --> 00:00:58.229
August 1979,

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:01.271
a 29-year-old man is called to a car by someone he apparently knows.

00:01:02.412 --> 00:01:03.193
Moments later,

00:01:03.293 --> 00:01:05.275
a shotgun rips a hole in his chest,

00:01:05.515 --> 00:01:06.596
and he's left to die.

00:01:08.218 --> 00:01:10.239
Had this crime occurred even a few years earlier,

00:01:10.399 --> 00:01:12.200
it would have merited front-page headlines.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.641
But by 1979,

00:01:14.643 --> 00:01:18.564
gang-related homicides were averaging almost one murder every 32 hours.

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:21.967
But the press apparently did not realize at the time.

00:01:22.384 --> 00:01:23.064
was that the victim,

00:01:23.164 --> 00:01:24.245
Raymond Lee Washington,

00:01:24.285 --> 00:01:27.064
was a founder of the notorious street gang called the Crips.

00:01:28.486 --> 00:01:31.507
Once a handful of teenagers dedicated to protecting the turf,

00:01:32.246 --> 00:01:32.487
by the

00:01:33.347 --> 00:01:39.429
1990s, Crips numbered in the tens of thousands and had expanded their criminal influence to wreak havoc throughout the United States.

00:01:40.849 --> 00:01:42.629
The story of the Crips begins in the early

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:47.971
1940s when the explosion of wartime industry triggered a major migration of workers from the South.

00:01:48.852 --> 00:01:50.032
By 1944...

00:01:50.296 --> 00:01:53.118
The black population of Los Angeles had more than doubled.

00:01:54.198 --> 00:02:02.224
Anti-minority covenants and whites-only deed provisions in place since the 1920s kept blacks from living outside of carefully prescribed regions.

00:02:02.865 --> 00:02:04.225
Overcrowding was severe.

00:02:05.445 --> 00:02:10.250
The first public housing projects erected in Watts were in part an attempt to alleviate the problem.

00:02:10.469 --> 00:02:12.771
But as the population continued to expand,

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:16.554
pressure mounted on surrounding white communities to change their practices.

00:02:17.153 --> 00:02:19.415
That pressure often erupted in violence.

00:02:24.563 --> 00:02:30.527
Blacks who ventured across the unmarked border were often attacked by teenage members of a new gang called the Spook Hunters,

00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:33.389
one of a handful of white gangs active at this time.

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:39.373
It was only natural for LA's newest residents to respond in kind.

00:02:40.294 --> 00:02:45.057
It was into this environment that a young Raymond Lee Washington and his family arrived from Texas.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.619
Born in 1953,

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:49.220
Raymond soon hooked up with the avenue.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.561
one of many gangs active at the time.

00:02:52.681 --> 00:02:53.021
In the 60s,

00:02:53.382 --> 00:02:53.762
we had,

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:54.021
like,

00:02:54.022 --> 00:02:54.241
you know,

00:02:54.242 --> 00:02:55.021
the Slausons,

00:02:55.062 --> 00:02:55.902
the Gladiators,

00:02:55.903 --> 00:02:56.802
the Businessmans,

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:58.343
the Rebel Routes,

00:02:59.204 --> 00:03:00.145
and basically,

00:03:00.205 --> 00:03:00.525
you know,

00:03:00.965 --> 00:03:01.545
back then,

00:03:02.605 --> 00:03:03.086
it wasn't,

00:03:03.086 --> 00:03:03.346
you know,

00:03:03.466 --> 00:03:03.665
like,

00:03:03.925 --> 00:03:04.665
real violent,

00:03:04.766 --> 00:03:05.067
you know.

00:03:05.447 --> 00:03:11.329
Greg Batman Davis would eventually become a founding member of the Crips and is one of the few still alive today.

00:03:11.909 --> 00:03:13.389
For the first time on television,

00:03:13.629 --> 00:03:17.472
his exclusive interview reveals the genesis of the gang from its inception...

00:03:17.868 --> 00:03:20.769
and provides a first-hand portrait of the modern gang world.

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:24.651
Batman has long since retired from the gangbanger lifestyle,

00:03:25.191 --> 00:03:25.711
but in the early

00:03:26.652 --> 00:03:30.893
1960s, he was a fledgling member of the businessmen and engaged in the battles of the day.

00:03:32.134 --> 00:03:33.274
You might have a gang fight,

00:03:33.275 --> 00:03:34.995
you might see bumper jacks sometimes,

00:03:34.996 --> 00:03:35.775
you might see chains,

00:03:35.776 --> 00:03:36.616
you might see a knife,

00:03:37.316 --> 00:03:38.096
but it wasn't basically,

00:03:38.156 --> 00:03:38.436
you know,

00:03:39.297 --> 00:03:40.777
you get in a gun and kill somebody,

00:03:40.797 --> 00:03:41.078
you know.

00:03:41.418 --> 00:03:47.000
The fights during that time period usually emerged over something such as a girlfriend.

00:03:47.243 --> 00:03:52.587
One of the blacks that lived in the east side started to break out of the central Vernon ghetto and move on the west side,

00:03:52.607 --> 00:03:55.048
which was considered a more affluent area at that time.

00:03:55.369 --> 00:03:55.609
You know,

00:03:55.629 --> 00:04:00.772
there was sort of this economic disparity between blacks who were able to move on the west side and blacks that weren't.

00:04:00.992 --> 00:04:05.856
So then you start to see this conflict expanding in numbers and in turfs.

00:04:06.116 --> 00:04:07.517
And I believe in 1960,

00:04:07.657 --> 00:04:10.779
there were about six homicides,

00:04:11.659 --> 00:04:13.981
which was considered a lot during that time period.

00:04:15.782 --> 00:04:16.824
Back then they had like

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:18.680
Zip guns and stuff like that,

