but you know at that time I was kind of still kind of young

00:04:24.362 --> 00:04:29.245
Didn't nobody want to show me how to how to make no zip gun so I had to figure it out

00:04:29.904 --> 00:04:31.205
I made a 38 zip gun.

00:04:31.685 --> 00:04:34.067
I made a 410 zip gun like I say,

00:04:34.086 --> 00:04:35.587
you know back then It wasn't too much,

00:04:35.588 --> 00:04:37.528
you know about no gun,

00:04:38.008 --> 00:04:38.248
you know,

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:39.868
because everybody was believing in fighting

00:04:40.469 --> 00:04:45.951
It soon became clear the South Central was in a decline the post-war economic boom was over

00:04:46.572 --> 00:04:48.353
Factories closed or relocated.

00:04:48.992 --> 00:04:55.317
And while a 1954 Supreme Court ruling against segregation had opened schools and other services to black families,

00:04:55.717 --> 00:04:58.019
the ruling had unintended consequences.

00:04:58.459 --> 00:05:00.000
After the 1954...

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:00.761
Supreme Court ruling,

00:05:01.161 --> 00:05:02.302
the housing opened up,

00:05:02.362 --> 00:05:03.141
schooling opened up,

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:09.307
so a lot of middle class people from the inner city were able to move out.

00:05:09.706 --> 00:05:12.988
And with them they took their middle class organizations,

00:05:13.009 --> 00:05:15.610
their middle class organizing capacities and so on,

00:05:16.031 --> 00:05:19.454
leaving in the inner city those who were less capable of doing those things.

00:05:19.994 --> 00:05:23.856
And the gap has been filled in part by the emergence of street gangs.

00:05:24.617 --> 00:05:24.918
Dr.

00:05:24.978 --> 00:05:28.060
Malcolm Klein has studied gang issues for close to 40 years.

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:34.064
He recently retired as a director of the Social Science Research Institute at the University of Southern California.

00:05:34.904 --> 00:05:35.344
His book,

00:05:35.404 --> 00:05:36.745
The American Street Gang,

00:05:37.086 --> 00:05:42.110
challenges assumptions made by media and law enforcement about gangs and how best to control them.

00:05:42.449 --> 00:05:44.872
When I started in 1962,

00:05:44.951 --> 00:05:46.874
there were about 50 cities across the country,

00:05:47.274 --> 00:05:49.194
cities or suburbs of large cities,

00:05:49.975 --> 00:05:51.596
that had a gang problem of some sort.

00:05:51.976 --> 00:05:52.858
By 1970,

00:05:52.918 --> 00:05:53.519
that had doubled.

00:05:53.538 --> 00:05:54.418
By 1980,

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.240
it had doubled again.

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:57.680
And then in the mid-80s and the 90s,

00:05:57.701 --> 00:05:58.800
it's just exploded.

00:05:59.161 --> 00:06:06.442
The most recent national survey done by the National Youth Gang Center lists about 4,000 jurisdictions,

00:06:06.562 --> 00:06:08.444
cities to small towns and rural areas,

00:06:08.744 --> 00:06:09.704
that have a gang problem.

00:06:09.804 --> 00:06:13.105
That's just an enormous explosion of this problem.

00:06:14.064 --> 00:06:15.466
By 1965,

00:06:15.466 --> 00:06:17.745
the seeds of that future had already been planted.

00:06:18.305 --> 00:06:19.307
On August 11th,

00:06:19.466 --> 00:06:23.468
California Highway Patrol arrested a South Central motorist for drunk driving.

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:31.225
What started as a minor skirmish exploded into six days of full-scale rebellion that came to be known as the Watts Riots.

00:06:37.011 --> 00:06:41.053
There is no evidence to suggest young Raymond participated in the violence.

00:06:41.113 --> 00:06:43.615
It is almost certain he witnessed the chaos.

00:06:43.956 --> 00:06:47.920
We had our hands on some of the major black gangs in the area at the time,

00:06:48.379 --> 00:06:51.762
and they didn't get involved in the Watts Riots until the third day,

00:06:51.963 --> 00:06:52.704
or the third night,

00:06:52.723 --> 00:06:53.124
in fact.

00:06:53.408 --> 00:06:54.149
And by and large,

00:06:54.188 --> 00:06:56.230
their involvement was going down and watching the scene.

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:57.490
In the end,

00:06:57.591 --> 00:06:58.572
four people were dead.

00:06:59.173 --> 00:07:00.553
Another thousand had been injured.

00:07:01.153 --> 00:07:11.021
A special governor's commission later identified major causes for the rebellion as including an absence of job opportunities for blacks and a resentment of the Los Angeles Police Department,

00:07:11.442 --> 00:07:11.843
then in his

00:07:12.362 --> 00:07:14.584
15th year of leadership under Chief William Parker.

00:07:15.725 --> 00:07:22.812
The commission echoed both the governor and L.A.'s district attorney at the time in criticizing Parker's strong-arm approach to law enforcement.

00:07:23.247 --> 00:07:26.310
which many South Central residents experienced firsthand.

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:27.389
In the early

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:30.391
60s, LAPD was run by Chief Parker,

00:07:30.393 --> 00:07:32.932
who was a tremendous reformed chief.

00:07:32.973 --> 00:07:35.754
He took what had been a notoriously nationally,

00:07:35.795 --> 00:07:39.177
notoriously corrupt department and turned it around extremely effectively.

00:07:39.776 --> 00:07:41.958
But it distanced itself from the community.

00:07:42.038 --> 00:07:46.201
This was especially true in South Central Los Angeles and in East Los Angeles.

00:07:47.081 --> 00:07:48.701
As the community started to rebuild,

00:07:48.961 --> 00:07:52.223
street gangs like the Slausons and the Gladiators all but disappeared.

00:07:52.983 --> 00:07:54.125
For the next four years,

00:07:54.324 --> 00:07:56.885
gang-related violence was practically non-existent.

00:07:57.445 --> 00:07:59.906
Shortly after the Watch Rebellion in 1965,

00:08:00.266 --> 00:08:07.089
there was a whole bunch of organizations and programs started in Los Angeles by the youths who used to be in these clubs.

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:09.310
And one of them was the Black Panther Party,

00:08:09.491 --> 00:08:11.471
which was originally founded in Oakland.

00:08:12.012 --> 00:08:12.132
L.A.

00:08:12.233 --> 00:08:15.553
started a chapter under a guy named Alprentice Carter,

00:08:15.733 --> 00:08:16.594
also known as Bunchy,

00:08:17.574 --> 00:08:19.015
and he was a Slauson member.

00:08:19.135 --> 00:08:21.096
a club that existed in Los Angeles from the

00:08:21.456 --> 00:08:22.116
50s throughout the early

00:08:22.556 --> 00:08:25.197
60s. So as he became the president of this chapter,

00:08:25.297 --> 00:08:28.718
it started to get a lot of youths involved in this new movement.

00:08:28.958 --> 00:08:29.938
While most of the U.S.

00:08:29.998 --> 00:08:31.179
condemned the Black Panthers'

00:08:31.219 --> 00:08:32.399
revolutionary agenda,

00:08:32.939 --> 00:08:37.400
their message of community-based independence struck a chord with the residents of South Central.

00:08:38.021 --> 00:08:39.701
And even though they were too young to join,

00:08:40.101 --> 00:08:42.942
it is likely Raymond and his cohorts absorbed the Panthers'

00:08:42.982 --> 00:08:45.963
rhetoric through rallies and outreach programs in the community.

00:08:46.183 --> 00:08:48.745
The Black Panthers was pushing brothers to go to school.

00:08:49.825 --> 00:08:51.666
They was feeding breakfast in the morning.

00:08:51.885 --> 00:08:53.125
We was having breakfast and stuff.

00:08:53.725 --> 00:08:54.267
Like I told you,

00:08:54.268 --> 00:08:55.246
I wanted to be a Panther,

00:08:55.326 --> 00:08:57.888
but it wasn't going down.

00:08:57.889 --> 00:08:59.108
My mother wouldn't let me be one.

00:08:59.587 --> 00:09:02.048
In late November of 1968,

00:09:02.049 --> 00:09:02.948
FBI Director J.

00:09:03.129 --> 00:09:10.532
Edgar Hoover issued a memo directing his agents to exploit all avenues of creating dissension within the ranks of the Black Panther Party.

00:09:11.372 --> 00:09:16.413
Hoover's strategy involved counterintelligence measures pitting the Panthers against the US organization,

00:09:16.894 --> 00:09:19.916
another black power movement under the leadership of Ron Karenga,

00:09:20.256 --> 00:09:22.176
creator of the Kwanzaa celebration.

00:09:23.497 --> 00:09:31.500
It was relatively easy for the FBI to flame the fires of rhetoric by fabricating documents and political cartoons seemingly generated by each side.

00:09:32.561 --> 00:09:37.043
These covert efforts helped turn an ongoing philosophical debate into a deadly battle.

00:09:38.643 --> 00:09:40.644
In January of 1969,

00:09:40.864 --> 00:09:46.812
Bunchy Carter and John Huggins were gunned down on the UCLA campus allegedly by members of the US organization.

00:09:47.754 --> 00:09:48.634
Many years later,

00:09:48.835 --> 00:09:54.082
a retired FBI agent came forward with claims that the Bureau had helped plan the assassination.

00:10:00.862 --> 00:10:09.744
The demise of the Black Panthers in Los Angeles was said to be yet another blow to a generation of black teenagers who'd witnessed many of their role models assassinated throughout the

00:10:10.805 --> 00:10:12.665
1960s. What I'm saying in so many words,

00:10:12.985 --> 00:10:16.586
they should have let the Panthers win on because there probably would have never been no Crips or no Bloods.

